WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.590
Mix ethanoic acid with ethanol, and
they react to form an ester and water.

2
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.510
ΔG⦵ for the reaction is negative,
so the forward reaction is favoured.

3
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.370
Yet however long you wait, the mixture
never turns completely into ester.

4
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:20.730
If ΔG⦵ is negative, why doesn't a
reaction go all the way to products?

5
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.370
In this mission, you'll separate
ΔG⦵ from ΔG for a real mixture,

6
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.170
and meet the reaction quotient.

7
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.590
You'll link ΔG⦵ to the
equilibrium constant,

8
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.770
and predict which way a mixture will go.

9
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.890
Your mission:

10
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.710
explain why a reaction with a
negative ΔG⦵ still stops short.
